window.SIGNIN_CHAPTERS=(window.SIGNIN_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51: Paperwork","paragraphs":["Inside the executive boardroom of the Apex Tower...","Apex Media’s seemingly miraculous securing of two hundred million dollars in commercial soundstage leases was merely the first influx of corporate funds. It was just the opening act.","Within a single morning, a historically dead asset had been fully monetized, pumping a staggering amount of liquid revenue directly into Apex’s previously strained coffers.","Before Jude Lawson’s hostile takeover, the board of directors had written off the Nanshan Media Park as a catastrophic failure, a bleeding wound that threatened to sink the studio’s quarterly earnings.","Now, with the lots sold out and the deposits collecting interest in escrow, the studio had reversed its financial trajectory...","Back in the Apex executive tower, the senior analysts were still debating how their new CEO had managed to orchestrate such a miracle.","\"He said he used our holdings to force the governor’s hand,\" Harper recalled, pacing the boardroom. \"But how? Did he deploy a fleet of high-powered lobbyists to the state capital? Did he submit a hundred-page economic assessment report that the legislature simply couldn’t ignore?\"","The analysts nodded in agreement.","To their minds, drafting a brilliant economic survey was the only logical way a private citizen could sway a sitting governor.","They would have been shocked to learn that Jude Lawson hadn’t written a single page of paperwork.","Two weeks prior, while Harper had assumed Jude was touring the abandoned backlots, Jude had actually been responding to a classified system order.","[System Task: Acquire Total Monopoly of Nanshan District Infrastructure.]","[Task Level: Critical Asset Expansion.]","[Task Progress: 0/100.]","Jude had recognized the immense potential of the industrial sector long before the tax credit was even a rumor.","Because the government had previously halted development, the surrounding real estate was universally considered toxic, driving property values down to literal pennies on the dollar!","Rather than begging politicians with economic reports, Jude simply made a handful of phone calls from the back of his Maybach.","He purchased every single prime acre of industrial land surrounding the media park!","Once he held the monopoly, Jude weaponized his other corporate assets...","He ordered the executives of Zenith Motors and his various shell conglomerates to publicly announce intentions to build multi-billion-dollar manufacturing hubs.","However, he threatened to move those manufacturing hubs to a tax-friendly state unless the local governor immediately reinstated the Nanshan commercial incentives.","Faced with the prospect of losing billions in private infrastructure and thousands of potential jobs, the state governor had no choice.","Trapped by Jude’s capital gravity, the city convened a closed-door session and restarted the Nanshan development plan overnight.","While the Apex employees assumed Jude was a master lobbyist, his true identity as a multi-industry titan remained safely obscured in the shadows.","Of course, not everyone in the city was willing to accept Jude’s growing omnipotence...","High above the financial district in a guarded penthouse, Maxwell Pierce was pacing his Persian rug.","\"It’s impossible!\" Maxwell shouted, throwing his tumbler against the wall. \"Jude Lawson did not coerce the state legislature!\"","The remaining board members of Pierce Studios watched their former Chairman unravel in denial.","\"There is only one explanation,\" Maxwell reasoned. \"Lawson was just incredibly lucky! The governor’s office was obviously planning to reboot the Nanshan development plan anyway, and Lawson just happened to stumble into the zoning meeting!\"","Maxwell pointed a shaking finger at his executives. \"It was dumb luck!\"","Regardless of Maxwell’s copium, the undeniable fact remained: Apex Media was now flush with cash, and Jude Lawson’s industry prestige was skyrocketing to untouchable heights.","Following his annihilation of Preston Vanguard in the e-sports arena, Jude’s Maybach pulled up to the curb outside Le Bernardin.","The world-renowned Michelin-starred restaurant had been entirely closed to the public.","Director Vance, Victoria Vance, Harper, Maya, and the newly enriched professional athletes of the Apex gaming division were already mingling.","Even the four defected players from Team Vanguard were sitting at the tables.","\"Mr. Lawson has arrived!\" Director Vance announced, stepping forward to pull out the head chair for the billionaire.","Was this the same reserved board director who had once viewed Jude’s takeover attempt with such suspicion and skepticism?","It was as if Director Vance was a different person...","Jude had fully anticipated this total shift in loyalty.","Now that he was generating hundreds of millions in profit and personally elevating their careers, their attitude had naturally transformed into worship.","\"Thank you, Director Vance,\" Jude said, a smile touching his lips as he took his seat at the head of the banquet.","Maya, the loyal General Manager, leaned over Harper’s shoulder at the table. \"Harper, the accounting division just ran the preliminary numbers on today’s total revenue. Do you have any idea how much capital Mr. Lawson routed into our holding accounts today?\"","Harper paused, a piece of caviar resting on her fork.","She knew the commercial leases were immense, but Jude’s gaming wager added a new layer of complexity.","\"Between the non-refundable Nanshan deposits and the offshore exhibition wager... it has to be close to three hundred million,\" Harper guessed, her heart beating slightly faster.","\"Three hundred million?\" Maya beamed, her eyes wide.","Harper set her fork down on the plate, her breath catching in her throat.","\"Mr. Lawson, please, allow me. I requested the chef prepare this white truffle risotto just for your side of the table. I wasn’t sure of your culinary preferences, but you must let me know what you desire, and I will ensure it is catered to the boardroom tomorrow.\"","Marcus Cole, the Vice President of Asset Management, was smiling so warmly his face looked as if it might crack.","He was leaning over the table, spooning the risotto onto Jude’s plate.","Jude allowed a smile to touch his lips. \"I don’t really have any fancy favorites when it comes to food, Marcus. Though, before I acquired my current portfolio, I enjoyed the simple street-level espresso from a café near my old university. Unfortunately, working in the upper echelons of this city means I rarely have the time to track it down.\"","Marcus Cole’s eyes lit up as if he had just been handed the nuclear launch button.","\"Consider it done, Mr. Lawson! I will dispatch an assistant to locate that exact café tomorrow morning. We’ll have their premium roast imported to the executive lounge. Let’s see if our baristas can match your university memories!\""]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52: A State Within a State","paragraphs":["An hour later, the extravagant celebration finally concluded.","Jude and Harper left the restaurant and returned via private elevator to the Apex executive penthouse to review the finalized Nanshan lease contracts.","As they stepped into the suite, Jude tossed his suit jacket over a chair.","\"Jude, I really must apologize for Marcus Cole’s behavior tonight,\" Harper said, rubbing her temples. \"You didn’t need to indulge his greed.\"","Jude smiled, unbuttoning his cuffs. \"Securing the loyalty of your asset managers is essential.\"","\"I suppose,\" Harper sighed. \"But I refuse to let the studio drain your private accounts for luxury perks. I’ll ensure the aviation expenses are deducted from the division’s quarterly profits. It’s just... the accounting won’t be finalized until Friday, so the studio will owe you the capital until then.\"","Jude nodded. He walked over to the conference table dominating the center of the penthouse and began organizing the stacks of lease contracts.","Harper watched him work, biting her lower lip.","She harbored a growing frustration toward that table.","She wanted him to stop operating like a financial machine for just one night and actually celebrate their victory intimately...","Harper’s dark eyes suddenly lit up.","A bold idea crossed her mind, and she almost laughed at her own audacity.","Jude turned away for a fraction of a second to check a notification on his phone.","Taking advantage of the brief distraction, Harper reached across the table toward her freshly poured cup of espresso.","The boiling black coffee cascaded across the table, thoroughly soaking the copies of the Nanshan commercial leases.","\"What happened?\" Jude asked, turning back around to see the mess.","\"Oh, I am so sorry!\" Harper gasped. \"I was just trying to move my cup, and the ceramic slipped right out of my hand. The contracts are soaked.\"","\"I see,\" Jude said. \"I suppose they are temporarily illegible.\"","Harper’s face flushed a deep crimson, and she couldn’t help but lower her gaze, playing up her embarrassment.","\"Since the files are ruined... I suppose we can’t really review any more work tonight, Jude. Why don’t we just...\"","She was fully prepared to suggest they abandon the boardroom entirely, pour two glasses of the vintage wine waiting in the penthouse kitchen, and relax together on the living room sofa.","But before the invitation could even leave her lips, she looked up and saw Jude picking up his tablet, ignoring the coffee-stained mess.","Harper blinked in confusion. \"Jude, where are you going?\"","Jude offered a smile. \"Don’t worry about the copies, Harper. The legal team uploaded the encrypted cloud backups to my secure server an hour ago. I’ll simply review the digital dossiers on my private jet during the flight to Tokyo tomorrow.\"","With that, he turned on his heel and cheerfully walked out of the penthouse, the double doors clicking shut behind him.","*Damn it!*","Harper was left standing alone in the silent penthouse, overwhelmed by his maddening focus.","...","Cruising smoothly at forty thousand feet aboard his custom-modified Gulfstream, Jude Lawson rested his oxfords on the ottoman and scrolled through the screen of his tablet.","The morning’s financial feeds were dominated by a single headline: thepublic implosion of the Sterling Media conglomerate.","Jude couldn’t help but admire the carnage unfolding on the screen...","The trap Harper had laid back at the Global Media Symposium had finally matured.","According to the leaked transcripts making the rounds on Wall Street, Chairman Sterling had attempted to salvage his shattered marriage during an emergency board meeting.","He had wept openly in front of his shareholders, pointing a trembling finger at his former secretary, Cassandra.","He claimed the young woman had blackmailed him into the affair, insisting that he was a victim of espionage and that he only loved his wife.","It was an Oscar-worthy performance of a man drowning in his own lies...","Unsurprisingly, Beatrice Sterling hadn’t bought a single syllable of his drunken apologies.","*If she seduced you, it’s only because you eagerly swallowed the bait,* Beatrice had reportedly told him in front of the entire board. *Don’t expect me to share a husband. Let’s see how glorious your media empire is without my family’s capital.*","With those chilling final words, she had immediately frozen her trust fund assets, severing Sterling Media’s primary credit line overnight.","Jude smirked, tapping the edge of his coffee cup.","He accessed his holding company’s secure trading portal.","Chairman Sterling had already suffered a humiliating public execution, but in Jude’s world, a wounded competitor needed to be eradicated.","With a few swift taps, Jude authorized a short position against Sterling Media’s remaining stock.","\"Leaving him with nothing but the clothes on his back,\" Jude said.","It was a satisfying end for a CEO who had attempted to bully his executives in public.","Suddenly, the red light on Jude’s phone began to blink.","He picked up the receiver. \"Lawson.\"","The caller was Ghost... appointed just a week ago as head of private security, a silent enforcer, and the spearhead of Jude’s expansion.","\"Mr. Lawson, it’s Ghost.\"","The deeprumble of Jude’s head of private security came through the secure channel.","Ghost wasn’t currently stationed at the Apex tower; Jude had deployed him to Washington, D.C., to handle a top-tier negotiation with the federal government.","\"Update me on the Aegis Initiative, Ghost,\" Jude commanded. \"Have the federal regulators capitulated to our territorial demands?\"","\"Not entirely, sir,\" Ghost replied. \"The Pentagon oversight committee is extremely hesitant. They still require a live demonstration of your proprietary cybersecurity architecture before they agree to any legal concessions.\"","Jude narrowed his eyes, gazing out the jet window at the endless expanse of clouds.","Jude sighed. \"Give them whatever demonstration they require. But ensure they understand our conditions are absolute.\"","\"Understood, Mr. Lawson.\"","...","Two thousand miles away, deep inside a fortified underground conference room in the nation’s capital, Ghost severed the satellite connection.","He placed the phone face down on the stainless steel table and looked across the room at his negotiating partners.","Sitting opposite Ghost was Director Hayes of the Department of Defense, flanked by a sharp-eyed intelligence operative wearing wire-rimmed glasses.","\"Well, Mr. Ghost?\" the operative asked, pushing the glasses up the bridge of his nose. \"What are your employer’s thoughts on our proposed testing parameters?\"","\"My employer has authorized the deployment of a beta version of the Aegis security grid,\" Ghost stated, folding his hands on the table. \"We can conduct a live-fire penetration test tomorrow morning. Choose whichever sector you desire.\"","The operative’s eyes widened slightly.","\"Tomorrow morning? You’re telling me Lawson Capital has already developed a military-grade cybersecurity framework capable of repelling our elite red teams?\"","Ghost said nothing.","Armed with the technological superiority granted by Jude’s system, constructing an impenetrable firewall was an effortless task...","Director Hayes leaned forward, exchanging a skeptical look with the operative.","\"Assuming this security system actually passes our live-fire stress test tomorrow, what exactly is Mr. Lawson demanding in exchange for the licensing rights?\"","Ghost’s expression remained stoic.","\"Mr. Lawson is not interested in standard licensing fees,\" Ghost declared. \"He guarantees that no foreign or domestic entity will ever breach your infrastructure without explicit authorization.\"","Ghost leaned slightly forward.","\"However, in exchange for this technology, the federal government must guarantee that Mr. Lawson’s newly acquired coastal estate will be recognized as sovereign corporate territory. No federal agency, state organization, or legal entity may, for any reason or in any form, expropriate ownership, execute eminent domain, or conduct unsanctioned raids upon his private property.\"","It was a staggering demand...","Ghost knew that Jude’s ultimate intention wasn’t merely to build a sprawling mansion; Jude was laying the legal groundwork to establish an autonomous corporate city, free from the jurisdiction of standard federal oversight!","For a private citizen to demand a non-commercial, sovereign enclave on domestic soil was unthinkable...","The intelligence operative remained silent for a long minute.","Finally, the operative pushed hisglasses up his nose once more.","\"As long as your proprietary system can repel our best hackers tomorrow morning,\" the operative said slowly, \"all of these territorial demands are fully negotiable.\""]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53: Taking the Fall","paragraphs":["The flashing red and blue strobes of the federal convoy reflected against the rain-slicked asphalt, slwly winding down the driveway until they vanished behind the gates...","\"Eleanor.\"","Harper stepped forward as she addressed Gregory Vance’s wife.","Harper’s eyes dropped to Eleanor’s swelling abdomen, a pang of sympathy tightening her chest.","Eleanor Vance possessed an elegant sort of beauty, but beneath that soft exterior was a spine of steel.","Despite just watching her husband being handcuffed and escorted into an armored SUV by the FBI, she hadn’t shed a single tear in front of the federal agents...","Her gaze had remained fixed on Gregory’s departing vehicle.","She turned to Harper and the older man standing beside her, managing a faint smile. \"You both came.\"","The storm was picking up, so Eleanor gestured for Harper and Director Arthur Vance to follow her inside the estate.","\"Maria, please take Julian upstairs to his playroom,\" Eleanor instructed the head housekeeper in a hushed tone.","The seven-year-old boy was clinging to the banister, his small shoulders shaking with sobs.","Once they were seated in the formal living room, Eleanor turned her attention to the older board member. \"Director Vance, I cannot express how grateful I am that you showed up today.\"","\"Don’t mention it, Eleanor. Gregory is blood,\" Director Vance said, though his face remained grim. \"I know exactly the kind of burden he carried for this family. This is going to be an incredibly brutal process, especially with the baby on the way.\"","Eleanor offered a nod, resting a hand on her stomach. She then shifted her gaze toward Harper. \"Harper, Gregory asked me to relay a message to you before the agents breached the door.\"","Harper leaned forward slightly, her pulse quickening. \"What did he say?\"","\"He said...\" Eleanor paused, taking a unsteady breath to compose herself. \"He said he’s deeply sorry that his actions against the Pierce family forced you to sever your relationship with Agent Thorne.\"","That single sentence was all it took for Harper’s carefully maintained corporate mask to slip...","Her eyes instantly burned with unshed tears.","Fighting back the wave of emotion, Harper fiercely shook her head. \"No. He didn’t force my hand. He didn’t.\"","\"You don’t need to carry that guilt, Harper,\" Eleanor said. \"Gregory began scrubbing the studio’s digital footprint the moment he sensed the Department of Justice shifting their focus. He took sole responsibility for the kidnapping of Donovan Pierce. The FBI obviously doesn’t believe he acted alone; they are desperate to find a paper trail linking the crime directly to Mr. Lawson. But Gregory ensured there is nothing left to find.\"","\"The federal sentencing is going to be severe,\" Eleanor continued, her voice trembling slightly. \"He knows the prosecution will push for maximum penalties to crack him. He told me to expect five to ten years in a minimum-security facility.\"","\"Eleanor, what are your immediate plans?\" Harper asked.","Eleanor’s gaze swept across the luxurious living room, her eyes heavy with sorrow. \"This is the sanctuary Gregory built for us. Legally, the federal asset forfeiture won’t touch it because it’s entirely in my name. But I simply cannot stay here right now, and with the Pierce syndicate still operating in the shadows, I don’t feel secure.\"","\"I have a few secondary properties closer to the financial district,\" Eleanor added. \"I’ll likely relocate there by the end of the week.\"","Hearing this, Harper immediately shook her head. \"Eleanor, I own an empty penthouse located within the Apex executive residential tower. I want you to move in there immediately. The building is patrolled by Mr. Lawson’s private security contractors around the clock. With you being pregnant, I refuse to let you stay anywhere less secure.\"","Director Vance chimed in. \"Harper is correct. As a board member, I can handle the legal defense, but I cannot manage your day-to-day security. Gregory took the fall to protect our corporate ecosystem. Do not give us a reason to worry about your safety.\"","Eleanor looked deeply at Harper. Slowly, she nodded in immense gratitude. \"Alright. I’ll pack a bag tonight.\"","\"Director Vance, there is one final matter I need you to handle,\" Eleanor said.","\"Name it, Eleanor. It’s already done.\"","\"Julian needs to be immediately transferred to a different private academy. The parents of his current classmates are all embedded in the financial sector; they already know about the federal raid. I will not allow my son to be crucified by elite gossip.\"","\"Consider it handled. I’ll pull the strings this afternoon,\" Director Vance promised.","They lingered for another hour, only standing up to leave when they noticed Eleanor’s exhaustion taking hold.","Stepping back outside the estate, Harper noticed the storm had finally broken...","Director Vance looked up at the sky. The clouds were slowly retreating, allowing a few harsh rays of sunlight to spill across the wet asphalt.","Suddenly, Director Vance’s demeanor shifted. \"Come on, Harper. Let’s take a drive. I want you to inspect the Nanshan Media Park renovations.\"","An hour later, Harper donned a sleek white hard hat and followed Director Vance through the newly acquired industrial lot.","\"This sector has been neglected for years,\" Director Vance explained, gesturing to the construction crews swarming the warehouses. \"Before the rival studios can move their equipment in, our engineering division has to conduct rigorous structural diagnostics. If we find any critical load-bearing failures or cut corners in the foundation, we have to tear them down and pour new concrete.\"","\"And if the original developers botched the subterranean infrastructure?\" Harper asked. \"Do we authorize a total demolition and rebuild from scratch?\"","Director Vance nodded approvingly. \"Absolutely. Mr. Lawson secured premium leases; we are legally obligated to deliver premium infrastructure. We have to ensure this complex is a state-of-the-art corporate hub.\"","But as she watched the machinery dig into the earth, Harper smiled a satisfied smile.","Only she and the top tier of Apex Media knew the truth...","The soundstages were irrelevant. Because Jude had blackmailed the governor into reinstating the Nanshan District tax credit, the underlying dirt of this industrial park was about to skyrocket in value.","Once the city officially announced the zoning permits, the real estate alone would be worth billions!"]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54: Investments","paragraphs":["Director Vance stopped mid-sentence, his head snapping toward the open loading dock.","Beside him, Harper and Julian Vance, the Director’s hotshot nephew and Apex Media’s newly appointed lead architectural engineer turned to watch the spectacle unfold.","Ablacked-out Koenigsegg Jesko hypercar cut through the construction zone.","Jude Lawson stepped out of the driver’s seat, adjusting the cuffs of his suit.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" Julian greeted. \"I was under the impression your private jet to Tokyo was scheduled for wheels-up at noon.\"","Jude walked up the loading ramp. \"My Tokyo associates can wait an extra hour, Julian. I found myself with a brief window of free time, so I decided to personally inspect my newest industrial acquisition.\"","Julian couldn’t help but scoff under his breath. \"The private airstrip is literally forty miles in the opposite direction, sir. You didn’t come to check on the soundstages. You just wanted to ensure no one else was monopolizing President Harper’s schedule.\"","Jude didn’t bother denying the accusation. Instead, he offered a smile. \"You are an architectural engineer, Julian. You should know better than anyone that the most valuable assets require constant, vigilant supervision. I simply prefer to keep a very close eye on my investments.\"","Director Vance, sensing the testosterone filling the room, quickly stepped forward to break the tension.","He cleared his throat and gestured toward the center of the soundstage. \"Well, Mr. Lawson, since you’re here, you might as well inspect the centerpiece of our upcoming flagship production.\"","Jude shifted his sharp gaze toward the middle of the warehouse, where a silk tarp was currently being pulled back by two logistics handlers.","Sitting in the center of the floor was a restored, pristine 1964 Aston Martin DB5.","It was an authentic, museum-grade piece of automotive history, acquired at auction for a staggering fifteen million dollars...","It was slated to be the hero vehicle for Apex Media’s upcoming spy thriller, a film designed to completely dominate the summer box office.","Jude walked around the perimeter of the vehicle, admiring the silver chrome and the immaculate leather interior.","He paused near the driver’s side door and looked over the roof at Harper.","\"An exceptional acquisition,\" Jude noted, raising an eyebrow. \"I assume you requested this to replace your current commuter car? It certainly fits your aesthetic, Harper.\"","Director Vance burst into a hearty laugh. \"Good god, no! If she drove this priceless museum relic through downtown traffic, I’d have a heart attack! Every single pothole would be a twenty-thousand-dollar suspension repair! The vehicle meant for actual, daily commuting is the armored Maybach parked by the security gates!\"","\"Move aside,\" Julian muttered, stepping past Jude with a clipboard in hand.","Trying to reassert his dominance, the young architect began directing the logistics team to secure the DB5 inside a specialized, climate-controlled transport container.","\"Do you require assistance securing the transport manifest, Julian?\" Jude asked, his tone dripping with mock graciousness.","\"No need, Mr. Lawson. I’m familiar with the structural tolerances of high-value freight.\" Julian replied, checking off boxes on his tablet.","Jude didn’t take offense...","He reached into his jacket pocket and withdrew a featureless obsidian card.","It was an encrypted corporate black card connected directly to his offshore liquidity pool.","\"Director Vance, I assume the fifteen million for the DB5 is still sitting in escrow?\" Jude asked, bypassing the young architect.","\"Yes, sir. The auction house is expecting the final wire transfer by five o’clock today,\" the older executive confirmed.","Jude handed the obsidian card to the logistics foreman. \"Bypass the studio’s accounting division. Charge the fifteen million directly to this account, then have the asset fully insured under Harper’s personal corporate portfolio.\"","Having successfully secured the asset and thoroughly demoralized the young architect, Jude turned back to Harper.","Harper checked her designer watch. It was already creeping past one o’clock. \"I need to get back to the executive tower, Julian. The city zoning committee is holding a preliminary hearing regarding the Nanshan permits at three. We can review the rest of your structural schematics tomorrow morning.\"","\"I’ll lock up the soundstage, Harper,\" Director Vance offered, waving them off. \"You two go ahead.\"","After Jude and Harper disappeared through the loading dock doors, Director Vance let out a sigh and turned to his nephew.","\"I told you to rein it in, Julian,\" the older executive scolded. \"You never stood a chance. You are a brilliant engineer, but Jude Lawson operates on an entirely different planetary scale. Trying to impress her while he’s in the room is suicide.\"","Julian threw his clipboard onto a nearby crate, his face flushed with bitter frustration. \"If you knew she was so exceptional, Uncle Arthur, why didn’t you set me up with her two years ago? Before that Wall Street predator bought the studio and locked her down?\"","Director Vance shook his head, refusing to entertain his nephew’s pathetic lament. \"Because two years ago, she was solely focused on saving this company from bankruptcy. And quite frankly, Julian, she would have eaten you alive.\"","Meanwhile, outside the soundstage, the arrangements were being finalized...","Since Harper had ridden to the site in Director Vance’s vehicle, she was currently without a ride back to the downtown tower.","Jude took the driver’s seat of the Koenigsegg Jesko, cleanly waving off his private chauffeur and instructing the security detail to follow at a discreet distance in the armored SUV.","Harper slid into the incredibly low passenger seat. The cockpit felt more like a fighter jet than a luxury automobile.","Jude pressed the ignition. The V8 engine roared to life.","He didn’t hesitate...","Jude engaged the transmission and the hypercar shot forward like a fired bullet, leaving the Nanshan Media Park far behind in a blur of concrete.","For the first few miles, Jude pushed the Koenigsegg, letting the horsepower dominate the open roads.","But as they merged onto the elevated highway approaching the downtown financial district, he eased off the throttle, allowing the hypercar to glide through the dense metropolitan traffic.","Harper watched the city skyline approaching, her brow furrowing slightly as she realized they were in the wrong lane.","\"The Apex executive tower is at the next exit, Jude,\" Harper noted. \"Where exactly are we going?\""]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55: Jealous Billionaire","paragraphs":["\"We are heading back to my private suite at the Apex tower,\" Jude replied, his eyes fixed on the traffic ahead. \"I require your company while I finalize the municipal zoning applications for the Nanshan lots.\"","Harper arched a manicured eyebrow, thoroughly confused. \"I was under the impression your private jet to Tokyo was scheduled for departure over an hour ago. Don’t you have a critical board meeting with the overseas logistics division?\"","\"The overseas executives can wait on the tarmac,\" Jude dismissed, as if keeping a dozen international billionaires on hold was standard operating procedure.","\"Besides, it won’t take long. Once the final municipal signatures are cleared, I’ll take you somewhere entirely off the grid for the evening.\"","Hearing the subtle promise in his tone, Harper felt a sudden thrill flutter in her chest.","She lifted her chin. \"I suppose I can sacrifice a few hours to ensure the studio’s real estate portfolio doesn’t collapse.\"","Despite her haughty tone, Jude caught the undeniable upward curve of her lips.","A satisfied smile spread across his own face. Without taking his eyes off the road, he reached across the carbon-fiber center console, enveloping her hand in his.","He traced the line of her knuckles with his thumb. Harper felt a jolt of heat rush up her arm, but she made no attempt to pull away.","Ten minutes later, the roar of the Koenigsegg Jesko announced their arrival in the subterranean VIP garage of the Apex Media executive tower...","Jude ignored the dropped jaws and terrified stares. He walked around the sleek hood of the Jesko, opening the dihedral door for Harper and thoughtfully placing a hand over the roofline to ensure she didn’t bump her head.","\"Let’s go,\" Jude murmured, handing the hypercar’s electronic fob to a trembling valet.","Harper could feel the intense glares burning into her back, but she had long since grown accustomed to the overwhelming gravity of Jude’s presence...","She walked by his side as he led her past the security checkpoints and into the biometric express elevator, taking them straight to the penthouse executive suite.","As the doors slid open on the top floor, a row of senior executive assistants immediately stood at rigid attention.","Harper offered the nervous women a warm smile.","Jude, however, noticed the exchange. His eyes darkened slightly as he guided Harper through the double doors of his private office.","The moment the doors clicked shut, sealing them inside the soundproof room, Jude’s demeanor shifted.","Before Harper could even take a step toward the conference table, Jude caught her wrist.","With a single motion, he pulled her flush against his chest, backing her against the glass wall overlooking the metropolis.","\"Are you always that incredibly generous with my staff?\" Jude murmured, his voice dropping an octave, laced with an edge of jealousy.","Harper’s breath hitched.","She looked up into his gaze, her mind flashing back to the ruined lease contracts and the tension of the previous night.","\"They... they coordinate my logistics,\" Harper managed to whisper, trying to keep her composure. \"It’s just basic corporate morale.\"","He didn’t give her another second to rationalize. Lowering his head, Jude finally closed the distance between them, kissing her with consuming authority.","By the time he finally pulled away, Harper was breathless, her eyes slightly hazy.","Jude lingered for a fraction of a second, his thumb brushing her lower lip, fighting the overwhelming urge to abandon the municipal paperwork entirely.","\"Sit on the sofa,\" Jude commanded, his voice still slightly rough. \"I’ll order your preferred espresso from the lobby.\"","Harper offered a dazed nod, slowly making her way to the couch in the center of the office.","\"If you require a distraction, the tablet is on the side table. The secure network is already authenticated,\" Jude noted, taking his seat behind his sprawling desk.","Harper picked up the tablet. The screen prompted her for a numerical passcode.","Without thinking, she handed it toward Jude. \"What’s the cipher?\"","\"Your birthday,\" Jude replied without looking up from his dual monitors.","Harper blinked in genuine surprise. She typed the six digits, and the encrypted home screen instantly unlocked.","\"Jude, please tell me you don’t secure your primary holding accounts with personal dates,\" Harper warned. \"Any half-decent corporate espionage team could crack it in seconds.\"","Jude chuckled. \"That specific tablet only contains raw media files and preliminary scripts. My actual offshore liquidity is protected by military-grade firewalls that not even the Pentagon can breach.\"","\"As long as you know the risks,\" Harper said, leaning back into the cushions. \"Focus on the municipal permits. I’ll review the daily cuts of the spy thriller.\"","Harper slipped on a pair of noise-canceling headphones, immersing herself in the footage of their upcoming blockbuster.","Across the room, Jude’s fingers flew across his keyboard, coordinating with his offshore legal teams, transferring massive sums of escrow capital, and bullying the city zoning committee into finalizing the Nanshan tax credit documentation.","Time slipped away in the penthouse...","By the time Jude transmitted the final binding municipal signature, the sun had already dipped below the city skyline.","Jude pushed his chair back from the desk. He stood up and crossed the carpet, stepping behind the sofa where Harper was still intently studying the digital footage.","He leaned down, resting his hands on her shoulders, and pressed a soft kiss to the curve of her neck. \"What has you so captivated?\"","Harper gasped slightly. \"I was just reviewing the final action sequence for the third act,\" Harper said, slipping the headphones off her ears. \"Have you finished dismantling the local government?\"","Jude rounded the sofa, sitting down beside her and wrapping an arm around her waist.","Jude nodded, his eyes trailing toward the windows. \"Are you ready to leave the tower?\"","\"I didn’t even realize the sun had set,\" Harper admitted, shaking her head.","\"The timing is flawless,\" Jude said, standing up and offering her his hand. \"I promised to take you off the grid tonight. Shall we?\"","Harper smiled, placing her hand in his, more than ready to discover exactly what the billionaire had planned next..."]}]);
